body:
(EDIT: I've updated line numbers. They changed since the posting of this issue.)

Ok, I read through the C++. I believe the crash initially occurs here:

https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/scene/main/node.cpp#L2906-L2910

After [instantiating the scene](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/scene/main/node.cpp#L2797), the internally copied MeshInstance3D nodes do not exist in the copy.

So... I could be wrong... but I *think*:

The children of the internal copied MeshInstance3D nodes - the StaticBody3D that is - end up getting added to [`hidden_roots`](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/scene/main/node.cpp#L2837) because they are the first nodes that appear that are not owned by the scene root (because the MeshInstance3D nodes *are* owned by the scene root; so they're skipped, and their children are checked).

Because of this, and because the parents of the StaticBody3D nodes (the MeshInstance3D nodes) *don't exist*, when the process attempts to duplicate these StaticBody3Ds (since they're in `hidden_roots`), [it fails to find where to put them in the new tree](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/scene/main/node.cpp#L2906).

But, for whatever reason, it was decided that, when this happens, the copy [fails completely](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/scene/main/node.cpp#L2890-L2891), instead of just skipping them.

-----

If this is true, then, is there a critical reason for which the copy needs to fail at this point?
Or would it be safe to change these lines to skip, instead of fail?

https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/scene/main/node.cpp#L2906-L2910
```diff
		Node *parent = node->get_node(get_path_to(E->data.parent));
		if (!parent) {
-			memdelete(node);
-			return nullptr;
+			continue;
		}
```
